.TH NAME 1 "YYYY-MM-DD" "scriptname" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
name \- one-line lowercase summary
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B name
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.P
.B name
.B \-f
\fIFILE\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B name
does one thing, described in a short paragraph. Mention defaults and any
external commands it depends on, e.g.\&
.BR ffmpeg (1)
and
.BR fzf (1).
.P
A second paragraph for details, edge cases, and side effects.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-f " FILE"
Operate on
.IR FILE .
.TP
.BI \-o " DIR"
Output directory. Default:
.IR ~/output .
.TP
.B \-n
Dry run. Print what would happen; change nothing.
.TP
.B \-h
Show a short help message and exit.
.SH BEHAVIOUR
.SS What it does
.IP \(bu 2
First behaviour bullet.
.IP \(bu 2
Second behaviour bullet.
.SS Requirements
.IP \(bu 2
.B ffmpeg
and
.B vainfo
(from
.BR libva-utils )
.SH EXAMPLES
Run with defaults:
.IP
.EX
name
.EE
.P
Custom input and output:
.IP
.EX
name \-f input.mkv \-o ~/Videos/out
.EE
.P
Show what would run without doing it:
.IP
.EX
name \-n \-f input.mkv
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Failure: bad options, missing input, or a dependency is unavailable.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/output
Default output directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR related-tool (1),
.BR other-script (1)
.SH BUGS
Known limitations go here; omit the section if there are none.
.SH AUTHOR
Written for local use.
